@startuml
title Digital Credential Presentation part 0 : verifier setup , once per verifier agency (SD-JWT VC , OpenID4VP 1.0 , Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0)

participant "Verifier Officer" as Officer
participant "<color:#white>Verifier as a Service Portal</color>" as VSys #6A1B9A
participant "<color:#white>VCVP Core</color>" as Core #3F51B5
participant "<color:#white>one-core (VP Engine)</color>" as VPEngine #chocolate
participant "<color:#white>one-core (VC Engine)</color>" as VCEngine #chocolate
participant "<color:#white>HSM (AWS KMS)</color>" as HSM #darkgoldenrod
participant "<color:#white>ETDA Trusted List (CDN)</color>" as Trust #0B2E6B

note right of Officer #wheat:[SPEC] Verifier Officer = staff of the verifier agency using the Verifier as a Service Portal\nsections 0 to 0.3 : the agency sets up once , before any verification request (VP part 1)

note over Officer,Trust #khaki: 0. Verifier Setup (once per verifier agency , not per request)
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Verifier organisation , verifier key and verifier DID are prepared in the setup phase , VCVP does not create them during verification\nThe verifier is registered with ETDA and listed in the Verifier Trusted List (ver.txt) with its public key , allowed claims and purposes\nTrusted issuers are decided by the Issuer Trusted List , the verifier does not configure them
note over VPEngine,HSM #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 12.2.1 G-07 (MAY)  verifier key in soft key , TEE / WSCD or HSM\n• 12.2.1 (MUST)  verifier public key in the Verifier Trusted List entry or a did:web DID document at /.well-known/did.json
note over VPEngine,HSM #wheat:[SPEC] the engine verifier DID resolves under a path , so the key is published in the Verifier Trusted List entry | verifier keys in AWS KMS
note over VPEngine,HSM #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VP 1.0\n• 8.3  the wallet encrypts the response to a key from client_metadata jwks\nNIST SP 800-57 Part 1 Rev. 5\n• 9.5.3.2  the more copies of a key , the more exposure
note over VPEngine,HSM #wheat:[SPEC] the verifier DID has a keyAgreement key in AWS KMS (KEY_AGREEMENT , not exportable) , the engine puts it in client_metadata and decrypts the response\nVCVP Core also decrypts the response with it to check the issuer before the engine (VP part 2 , section 7.2) | no copy of the private key
note over VPEngine,HSM #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 8.1.2 (MUST)  create and verify EdDSA and ES256\n• 11.2 (MUST)  issuers and verifiers accept both
note over VPEngine,HSM #wheat:[SPEC] AWS KMS key specs : ECC_NIST_P256 (ES256) , ECC_NIST_EDWARDS25519 (Ed25519 , signing only)
note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 9.8 (MUST)  identity , key , status , validity period and scope checked from the Trusted List\n• page 12.1 , 12.1.4 (MUST)  reject the trust decision when they cannot be confirmed\n• page 12.1 , 12.1.6 (MUST NOT)  a list without status or scope is not used for real
note right of Core #FFCDD2:[PENDING] waiting for ETDA | Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\nissue : no fields yet for entity and service status , validity period , VC types of issuers , allowed claims , purposes and wallet type (9.8 , 12.1.4)\nquestion : which fields will list them , and when
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] decided by ETDA after discussion : these Trusted List fields are phase 2 work , not in phase 1
note right of Core #B3E5FC:[WORKAROUND] until ETDA publishes these fields , a missing field does not reject the transaction (12.1.4 MUST reject)\nremove when the fields are published (phase 2) , the checks in these diagrams then use them

note over Core,Trust #violet: 0.1 Load ETDA Trusted Lists (when a transaction needs them)
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] steps in the ETDA Trusted List Load sequence (first tab)\nVCVP Core also loads ver.txt for its own verifier check in VP part 1 section 2
note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• appendix 8.2 E.1.1 (MUST)  the verifier fetches iss.txt and wp.txt
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Trusted List not usable (TRUST_LIST_EXPIRED / TRUST_LIST_UNAVAILABLE) : the calling step answers 503 Service Unavailable + Retry-After: 300\nnot the trust failure reason of that step , as in the ETDA Trusted List Load sequence

note over Officer,VPEngine #khaki: 0.2 Find the published schema of the issuer (CredentialSchemas table of VCVP)
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] the CredentialSchemas table holds the schemas that issuers on this VCVP created at VCVP Core 05 (Status = ACTIVE)\nschemas of other systems are added to this table by the VCVP administrator , procedure not designed yet
note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 9.8 (MUST)  scope of an issuer = VC types and claims it may issue , checked from the Trusted List
note right of Core #B3E5FC:[WORKAROUND] VCVP Core 46 searches schemas in the CredentialSchemas table of VCVP (Status = ACTIVE , no engine call)\nbecause the Trusted List has no credential types per issuer yet (Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0 9.8 , ETDA moved it to phase 2) and there is no central credential schema registry to search (3.3 , no ETDA API yet)\nremove this endpoint when ETDA publishes credential types in the Trusted List or a central credential schema registry , together with the [WORKAROUND] step of VCVP Core 22
Officer->VSys: Search the published schemas (issuer , credential type , vct)
VSys->Core: List published schemas + Consumer-Key + Token | GET /api/credential-schema/v1/published (VCVP Core 46)\nissuer_org_code (optional) , credential_type_name (optional) , ecosystem_schema_id (optional)
Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key and Token , caller channel , ActorType = OFFICER\nvalidate caller authorization
alt Consumer-Key or Token invalid or missing
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 46 (FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED , OrgCode and Actor empty)
    VSys<--Core: 401 + WWW-Authenticate | failure_reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED
    Officer<--VSys: Show error , no schemas shown
else Caller not authorized
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 46 (FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED)
    VSys<--Core: 403 | failure_reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    Officer<--VSys: Show error , no schemas shown
else Caller authorized
    Core->Core: Read CredentialSchemas (Status = ACTIVE) of the issuer organisations , filtered by the query , no match gives an empty list\nnames of the schema from CredentialSchemas , OrgCode and name of the issuer from Organizations\nCredentialTypes only to match credential_type_name (NameEn or NameLocal)\necosystem_schema_id matches Formats[].EcosystemSchemaId exactly (every character) , the result may list several organisations
    Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 46 : who searched the published schemas , with the query
    VSys<--Core: 200 | items [ org_code , organization_name , credential_type_id , name_en , name_local ,\ncredential_schema_id , formats [ format , ecosystem_schema_id ] ]
    Officer<--VSys: Published schemas of the issuers
end
Officer->VSys: Choose one schema to verify (CredentialSchemaId)

note over Officer,VPEngine #khaki: 0.2.1 Import the published schema of the issuer
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] VCVPAuditLog for every request , also those rejected at the Consumer-Key check (OrgCode and Actor empty) , kept 7 years
note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 8.6 , 8.8 (MUST)  audit log at least 7 years
Officer->VSys: Import the chosen schema
VSys->Core: Import schema + Consumer-Key + Token | POST /api/credential-schema/v1/import (VCVP Core 22)\norg_code , source_credential_schema_id
Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key and Token , caller channel , ActorType = OFFICER\nvalidate caller authorization
note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] RFC 9110\n• 15.5.2 (MUST)  401 when the request has no valid credentials , with WWW-Authenticate\n• 15.5.4  403 when the caller is known but not allowed
alt Consumer-Key or Token invalid or missing
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 22 (FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED , OrgCode and Actor empty)
    VSys<--Core: 401 + WWW-Authenticate | failure_reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED
    Officer<--VSys: Show error , schema not imported
else Caller not authorized
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 22 (FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED)
    VSys<--Core: 403 | failure_reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    Officer<--VSys: Show error , schema not imported
else Caller authorized
    Core->Core: Map OrgCode to OrganizationId (Organizations)
    note right of Core #B3E5FC:[WORKAROUND] the verifier imports only schemas in the CredentialSchemas table of VCVP , found with VCVP Core 46 : no central credential schema registry yet (Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0 3.3 , no ETDA API)\nand no credential types per issuer in the Trusted List yet (9.8 , ETDA moved it to phase 2)\nremove when ETDA publishes a credential schema registry or credential types in the Trusted List , together with VCVP Core 46
    Core->Core: Find source_credential_schema_id in CredentialSchemas table (Status = ACTIVE)\nEngineId , OrgCode of the issuer (Organizations) , IssuingSystem = VCVP (for Source)
    alt Source schema not in CredentialSchemas or not ACTIVE
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 22 (FailureReason = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND)
        VSys<--Core: 403 | failure_reason = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND
        Officer<--VSys: Show error , schema not imported
    else Source schema found in CredentialSchemas
    Core->Core: Find ImportedCredentialSchemas row of the caller organisation (OrganizationId)\nwith Source.CredentialSchemaId = source_credential_schema_id and Status = ACTIVE
    note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] RFC 9110\n• 15.5.10  409 Conflict , conflict with the current state of the resource , the user can resolve it and resubmit
    alt Already imported
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 22 (FailureReason = SCHEMA_ALREADY_IMPORTED)
        VSys<--Core: 409 | failure_reason = SCHEMA_ALREADY_IMPORTED
        Officer<--VSys: Show error , schema already imported
    else Not imported yet
    Core->VCEngine: Get the source schema from the issuer engine | GET /ssi/schema/v2/{id}
    alt Source schema not found (engine BR_0006)
        VCEngine-->Core: 404 BR_0006
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 22 (FailureReason = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND , EngineCalls)
        VSys<--Core: 403 | failure_reason = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND
        Officer<--VSys: Show error , schema not imported
    else Source schema found
    VCEngine-->Core: schema (formats[].ecosystemSchemaId , claims[] key , mappings.technicalKey)
    Core->VCEngine: Get the type metadata | GET /ssi/vct/v2/{organisationId}/{credentialSchemaId}/{format} (same engine endpoint as VCVP Core 18)
    VCEngine-->Core: type metadata document
    note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] SD-JWT VC draft-19\n• 5.3.1  type metadata retrieved from the URL in vct (HTTP GET)\n• 5.2 (REQUIRED)  vct in the type metadata document\n• 5.3 (MUST)  vct in the reference identical to the vct of the credential\n• 5.3 (MUST)  vct#integrity is an integrity metadata string (section 6)\n• 6  hash of the type metadata document octets
    Core->Core: Check vct in the document = the vct used to fetch it (Formats[].EcosystemSchemaId of the source schema)
    alt Type metadata not retrieved or vct does not match
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 22 (FailureReason = TYPE_METADATA_UNAVAILABLE , EngineCalls)
        VSys<--Core: 502 | failure_reason = TYPE_METADATA_UNAVAILABLE
        Officer<--VSys: Show error , schema not imported
    else Type metadata matches
    Core->Core: TypeMetadataIntegrity = sha256 of the document octets (sha256-... as in vct#integrity)
    Core->VPEngine: Import schema into the verifier organisation | POST /api/credential-schema/v2/import
    alt A schema with the same vct already exists in the verifier organisation (engine BR_0007)
        VPEngine-->Core: 400 BR_0007
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 22 (FailureReason = SCHEMA_ALREADY_IMPORTED , EngineCalls)
        VSys<--Core: 409 | failure_reason = SCHEMA_ALREADY_IMPORTED
        Officer<--VSys: Show error , schema already imported
    else Imported
    VPEngine-->Core: id
    Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Store ImportedCredentialSchemas table (ImportedCredentialSchemaId = id , OrganizationId , Source ,\nTypeMetadataIntegrity , EngineId , Status = ACTIVE)
    Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 22 : who imported which issuer schema (EngineCalls)
    VSys<--Core: 200 | imported_credential_schema_id
    Officer<--VSys: Schema imported
    end
    end
    end
    end
    end
end

note over Officer,VPEngine #khaki: 0.2.2 Read the imported schema (claims to choose)
Officer->VSys: Open the imported schema to choose the claims to request
VSys->Core: Get imported schema claims + Consumer-Key + Token | GET /api/credential-schema/v1/imported/{imported_credential_schema_id} (VCVP Core 45)
Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key and Token , validate caller authorization\nFind ImportedCredentialSchemaId in ImportedCredentialSchemas table (Status = ACTIVE)\nCheck the caller has an ACTIVE OrgRole in ImportedCredentialSchemas.OrganizationId
alt Consumer-Key or Token invalid or missing
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 45 (FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED , OrgCode and Actor empty)
    VSys<--Core: 401 + WWW-Authenticate | failure_reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED
    Officer<--VSys: Show error , claims not shown
else Imported schema not found or not ACTIVE
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 45 (FailureReason = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND)
    VSys<--Core: 403 | failure_reason = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND
    Officer<--VSys: Show error , claims not shown
else Caller has no ACTIVE OrgRole in the organisation that owns the schema
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 45 (FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED)
    VSys<--Core: 403 | failure_reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    Officer<--VSys: Show error , claims not shown
else Schema found
    Core->VPEngine: Get imported schema | GET /api/credential-schema/v2/{id}
    VPEngine-->Core: schema (claims[] key , datatype , required , translations , mappings)
    Core->Core: source and status from ImportedCredentialSchemas , type_metadata_integrity of the SD_JWT_VC format from TypeMetadataIntegrity\nversion and claims[].data_category from CredentialSchemas (row = Source.CredentialSchemaId , claim matched by Path = claims[].key)
    Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 45 : who read which imported schema (EngineCalls)
    VSys<--Core: 200 | created_date , last_modified , org_code , source ,\nname_en , name_local , description_en , description_local , version , formats ,\nsuspendable , revocable , requires_wallet_instance_attestation , key_storage_security , claims , status
    Officer<--VSys: Claims that can be requested
end

note over Officer,VPEngine #khaki: 0.3 Define what to request (verification template)
Officer->VSys: Define verification template (claims to request , chosen from the result of VCVP Core 45)
VSys->Core: Create verification template + Consumer-Key + Token | POST /api/proof-schema/v1 (VCVP Core 23)\norg_code , name_en , name_local , expire_duration_sec , inputs [ imported_credential_schema_id , claims ]
Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key and Token , validate caller authorization
alt Consumer-Key or Token invalid or missing
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 23 (FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED , OrgCode and Actor empty)
    VSys<--Core: 401 + WWW-Authenticate | failure_reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED
    Officer<--VSys: Show error , template not created
else Caller not authorized
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 23 (FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED)
    VSys<--Core: 403 | failure_reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    Officer<--VSys: Show error , template not created
else Caller authorized
    Core->Core: Map org_code to OrganizationId (Organizations) , not found 403 FailureReason = ORGANISATION_NOT_FOUND
    Core->Core: Find ImportedCredentialSchemas of each inputs[] (Status = ACTIVE)\nnot found or OrganizationId of the row is not the OrganizationId of org_code : 403 FailureReason = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND\nCheck the caller has an ACTIVE OrgRole in ImportedCredentialSchemas.OrganizationId , otherwise 403 FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    Core->VPEngine: Get imported schema | GET /api/credential-schema/v2/{id}
    VPEngine-->Core: schema (claims[] id , key)
    Core->Core: Check the requested claims exist in claims[].key of that schema , otherwise 400 FailureReason = REQUEST_REJECTED
    Core->Core: Check expire_duration_sec : when sent , an integer from 1 to the maximum claim retention (VCVP setting , default 3600 seconds) , otherwise 400 FailureReason = REQUEST_REJECTED\nnot sent : the default claim retention (VCVP setting)
    note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 7.2 item 3  the wallet enforces the purposes and allowed claims of the verifier\n• appendix 8.2 E.1.5 (MUST)  claims path and purpose within the scope allowed for the verifier , otherwise rejected
    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] decided by ETDA after discussion : checking the requested claims against ver.txt is phase 2 work , not done in phase 1
    Core->Core: Check the requested claims are within the claims allowed for this verifier in the Verifier Trusted List (ver.txt)
    note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 7.7 item 3 (MUST)  check the schema version , not the type name only
    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] the vct contains the schema id , a new schema version is a new schema with a new vct and new type metadata\nthe vct and vct#integrity of the presented credential are checked in VP part 2 , section 7.2
    note right of VPEngine #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] expireDuration is how long the engine keeps the received claim values after the check\n(retainUntilDate = completedDate + expireDuration , the engine deletes them only when its retention task is run , VCVP does not run it)\nIt is not the lifetime of the verification link (the link lives 1 hour)
    note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] RFC 9901 (SD-JWT)\n• 10.2 (SHOULD NOT)  after verification the verifier does not store the issuer-signed JWT or the disclosures
    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] expireDuration = the maximum claim retention (VCVP setting , default 3600 seconds) , not expire_duration_sec\nexpire_duration_sec = seconds the claim values are kept after their first delivery (VCVP Core 32) , then VCVP Core 48 deletes them (VP part 2 , section 9.2)
    Core->VPEngine: Define verification requirements | POST /api/proof-schema/v1\nname , organisationId , expireDuration , proofInputSchemas [ credentialSchemaId , claimSchemas [ id , required ] ]
    VPEngine-->Core: id
    Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Store VerificationTemplates table (VerificationTemplateId = id from the engine , ExpireDurationSec)
    Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 23 (EventType = VERIFICATION_TEMPLATE_CREATED) : who created which verification template (EngineCalls)
    VSys<--Core: 200 | verification_template_id
    Officer<--VSys: Verification template ready
end

@enduml
